525	    /// of [`PROBE_GROUP_PAIRS`] back-to-back timer pairs (empty
526	    /// timed intervals) and summarize the per-pair distribution.
527	    ///
528	    /// - `since` anchors [`ProbeSummary::t_start_s`], so every
529	    ///   probe in a run shares one time origin.
530	    /// - The floor is a low quantile, not the minimum: it rejects
531	    ///   one-sided interference (preemption only ever inflates a
532	    ///   group) while staying off the exact edge.
533	    /// - **Two resolutions on purpose.** Floor, spread, drift and
534	    ///   step read *group* means, where the timer's 1 ns quantum
535	    ///   is ~0.06% of a ~1.6 µs group rather than ~4% of a single
536	    ///   pair. The census instead counts *individual* pairs,
537	    ///   because a group mean hides anything smaller than
538	    ///   ~800 ns — an intrusion has to survive being averaged
539	    ///   over 64 pairs to register. A census threshold sits far
540	    ///   above the 1 ns quantum, so counting pairs costs the
